  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've noticed people getting banned in public instances for using avatars with content warning labels. Adult content avatars aren't allowed in public instances, so why are players allowed to use them there in the first place?\n\nPublic instances should entirely disallow avatars with content warning labels. This way, players wouldn't encounter issues because the VRChat API wouldn't allow the use of such avatars in public.\n\nImplementing this would be an effective way to enforce community guidelines\n\n＜＞＜",
